<div id="A2.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Discussion on a new notion of per-token quality.</span>
Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Provable guarantee of PRISM-extension). ‣ B.3 Extension on PRISM’s provable guarantee ‣ Appendix B Training algorithms and guarantees of PRISM ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> guarantees that the minimizer of the extended PRISM loss satisfies</p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0.625,0.5273}g_{\phi^{\star}}^{i}({\mathbf{y}})}=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{S}\sim\Pi(\cdot\mid{\mathbf{y}},i)}\left[p({\mathbf{x}}^{i}={\mathbf{y}}^{i}\mid{\mathbf{y}}\oplus\mathbf{m}_{\mathcal{S}})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">g</mi><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">⋆</mo></msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">i</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">𝐲</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0.625,0.5273}g_{\phi^{\star}}^{i}({\mathbf{y}})}=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{S}\sim\Pi(\cdot\mid{\mathbf{y}},i)}\left[p({\mathbf{x}}^{i}={\mathbf{y}}^{i}\mid{\mathbf{y}}\oplus\mathbf{m}_{\mathcal{S}})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Note that by construction, we always have <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. This encompasses the <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> case in Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Theoretical foundation of PRISM ‣ 3 PRISM ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>; When <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the posterior distribution <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pi(\cdot\,|\,{\mathbf{y}},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi(\cdot\,|\,{\mathbf{y}},i)</annotation></semantics></math> collapses to a point mass at <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\{i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\{i\}</annotation></semantics></math>, recovering Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (PRISM). ‣ 3.1 Theoretical foundation of PRISM ‣ 3 PRISM ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">However, we emphasize that this extended definition still captures our <em id="A2.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">intended</em> notion of per-token quality—namely, the (posterior) likelihood of <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> given the rest of the context, here defined under a certain distribution over <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}\oplus\mathbf{m}_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}\oplus\mathbf{m}_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>. (note that always <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>). Consequently, a model fine-tuned with the (extended) PRISM loss retains the capacity to identify low-quality tokens, while allowing <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> to average over multiple plausible masked-context views of <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">’s effect on PRISM.</span> We show in Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (PRISM). ‣ 3.1 Theoretical foundation of PRISM ‣ 3 PRISM ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Provable guarantee of PRISM-extension). ‣ B.3 Extension on PRISM’s provable guarantee ‣ Appendix B Training algorithms and guarantees of PRISM ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> that, as intended, the design of (b), in which we use <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, does not directly influence our theoretical results. To clarify, when <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the minimizer <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi^{\star}}^{i}({\mathbf{y}})\;=\;p\!\left({\mathbf{x}}^{i}={\mathbf{y}}^{i}\,\middle|\,{\mathbf{y}}\oplus\mathbf{m}_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.333em;" width="0.333em"><mi>p</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi^{\star}}^{i}({\mathbf{y}})\;=\;p\!\left({\mathbf{x}}^{i}={\mathbf{y}}^{i}\,\middle|\,{\mathbf{y}}\oplus\mathbf{m}_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> remains fully independent from <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> (or the rule for choosing <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>), and when <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, the only change is indirect: <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> (and the rule for choosing index set <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> during PRISM fine-tuning) affects the posterior over masked sets <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pi(\cdot\mid{\mathbf{y}},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi(\cdot\mid{\mathbf{y}},i)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Practically, <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A2.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">shapes</em> the training distribution of samples <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{y}},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{y}},i)</annotation></semantics></math>
observed during PRISM fine-tuning, potentially aligning it with those encountered at inference. Since the PRISM loss supervises <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is sampled from <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is likely to be seen at the inference time (since we also use <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> during inference to sample clean tokens). We hypothesize that this alignment improves PRISM fine-tuning, and we revisit this point with an ablation on OpenWebText (Appendix <a href="#A4.SS4" title="D.4 Ablation on Fine-tuning Hyperparameters-Nucleus sampling ‣ Appendix D Experiment details and ablation studies ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Employing PRISM at inference</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide details and pseudocode of inference algorithms that we use for our experiments. We first recall from Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Employing PRISM at inference ‣ 3 PRISM ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> how PRISM fine-tuned model (<math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta},g_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta},g_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>) is used at inference: At each step <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> through the following steps.</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:17pt;">
<li id="A3.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Choose a subset of masked tokens <math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> to <span id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;--ltx-bg-color:#ECF0FC;">unmask</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Choose a subset of clean tokens <math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> to <span id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;--ltx-bg-color:#E6F5F3;">remask</span>  with the lowest quality scores <math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;--ltx-bg-color:#E6F5F3;">remask</span>  <math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and for each <math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;--ltx-bg-color:#ECF0FC;">unmask</span>  <math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to a clean token sampled from <math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{\theta}^{j}(\cdot\,|\,{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}})\in\Delta(\mathcal{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}^{j}(\cdot\,|\,{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}})\in\Delta(\mathcal{V})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We now provide the pseudocode for two different cases of PRISM implementation, depending on how we choose the sizes of the unmasking and remasking sets <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{T}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{T}|</annotation></semantics></math>. We begin with the case where we stochastically assign <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{T}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{T}|</annotation></semantics></math> from binomial distributions (Algorithm  <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Employing PRISM at inference ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), corresponding to our experiments on OpenWebText (Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Unconditional Text Generation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> PRISM inference with assignments from binomial distributions</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Require:</span> Fine-tuned MDM with unmasking posterior model <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, per-token quality head <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, discretized time steps <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{t_{\ell}\}_{\ell=0}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{t_{\ell}\}_{\ell=0}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>,
sampling steps <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, sequence length <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, remasking token ratio <math id="alg2.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          Initialize <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{1}={\mathbf{x}}_{t_{1}}\leftarrow(\mathbf{m},\dots,\mathbf{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{1}={\mathbf{x}}_{t_{1}}\leftarrow(\mathbf{m},\dots,\mathbf{m})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-1</annotation></semantics></math> 

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\sim\mathrm{Binom}(|\{i\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}^{i}\neq\mathbf{m}\}|\,,\,\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Binom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\sim\mathrm{Binom}(|\{i\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}^{i}\neq\mathbf{m}\}|\,,\,\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> and define <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}\leftarrow\{i\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}^{i}=\mathbf{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}\leftarrow\{i\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}^{i}=\mathbf{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\leq|\mathcal{M}|&lt;L-K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\leq|\mathcal{M}|&lt;L-K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\geq l_{on}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\geq l_{on}</annotation></semantics></math>: 

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{T}|\leftarrow K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{T}|\leftarrow K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|\leftarrow\lceil\frac{L}{N_{s}}\rceil+K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|\leftarrow\lceil\frac{L}{N_{s}}\rceil+K</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>:

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{T}|\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{T}|\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|\leftarrow\lceil\frac{L}{N_{s}}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|\leftarrow\lceil\frac{L}{N_{s}}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>
  
</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
            Sample <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\subset\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\subset\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> according to the unmasking rule

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
            Sample <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}\subset\{i\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}^{i}\neq\mathbf{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}\subset\{i\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}^{i}\neq\mathbf{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with low-<math id="alg2.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{T}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{T}|</annotation></semantics></math> indices of <math id="alg2.l10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0.625,0.5273}g_{\theta}^{\cdot}(x_{t_{\ell}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">⋅</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">x</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0.625,0.5273}g_{\theta}^{\cdot}(x_{t_{\ell}})}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l11.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;">Unmask</span> <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{i}_{t_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{i}_{t_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v^{i}\sim{\color[rgb]{0.2539,0.4102,0.8828}f_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\,|\,{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">i</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#4169E1">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" fence="false" mathcolor="#4169E1" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">𝐱</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{i}\sim{\color[rgb]{0.2539,0.4102,0.8828}f_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\,|\,{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}})}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="alg2.l11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l12.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;">Remask</span> <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{j}_{t_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{j}_{t_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="alg2.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell+1}}\leftarrow{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell+1}}\leftarrow{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{N}}={\mathbf{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{N}}={\mathbf{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we state the algorithm where we pre-allocate <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{T}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{T}|</annotation></semantics></math> before inference (Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ Appendix C Employing PRISM at inference ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) with fixed <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponding to our experiments on Sudoku <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Motivating example: Sudoku puzzle ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> and LLaDA <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Appyling PRISM to 8B MDM ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> PRISM inference with fixed <math id="alg3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg3.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Require:</span> Fine-tuned MDM with unmasking posterior model <math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, per-token quality head <math id="alg3.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, sampling steps <math id="alg3.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, sequence length <math id="alg3.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, discretized time steps <math id="alg3.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{t_{\ell}\}_{\ell=0}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{t_{\ell}\}_{\ell=0}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, number of remasking tokens <math id="alg3.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          Initialize <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{1}={\mathbf{x}}_{t_{1}}\leftarrow(\mathbf{m},\dots,\mathbf{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{1}={\mathbf{x}}_{t_{1}}\leftarrow(\mathbf{m},\dots,\mathbf{m})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg3.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg3.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-1</annotation></semantics></math> 

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            Define <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}\leftarrow\{i\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{l}}=\mathbf{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}\leftarrow\{i\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{l}}=\mathbf{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg3.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\leq|\mathcal{M}|&lt;L-K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\leq|\mathcal{M}|&lt;L-K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg3.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\geq l_{on}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\geq l_{on}</annotation></semantics></math>: 

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{T}|=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{T}|=K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg3.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|=\lceil\frac{L}{N}\rceil+K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|=\lceil\frac{L}{N}\rceil+K</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg3.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>:

</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg3.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{T}|=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{T}|=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg3.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|=\lceil\frac{L}{N}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|=\lceil\frac{L}{N}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>
  
</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
            Sample <math id="alg3.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\subset\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\subset\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> according to the unmasking rule

</div>
<div id="alg3.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
            Sample <math id="alg3.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}\subset\{i\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}^{i}\neq\mathbf{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}\subset\{i\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}^{i}\neq\mathbf{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with low-<math id="alg3.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{T}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{T}|</annotation></semantics></math> indices of <math id="alg3.l10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0.625,0.5273}g_{\theta}^{\cdot}(x_{t_{\ell}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">⋅</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">x</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0.625,0.5273}g_{\theta}^{\cdot}(x_{t_{\ell}})}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg3.l11.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;">Unmask</span> <math id="alg3.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{i}_{t_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{i}_{t_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg3.l11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v^{i}\sim{\color[rgb]{0.2539,0.4102,0.8828}f_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\,|\,{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">i</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#4169E1">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" fence="false" mathcolor="#4169E1" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">𝐱</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{i}\sim{\color[rgb]{0.2539,0.4102,0.8828}f_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\,|\,{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}})}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="alg3.l11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg3.l12.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;">Remask</span> <math id="alg3.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{j}_{t_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{j}_{t_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="alg3.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg3.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell+1}}\leftarrow{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell+1}}\leftarrow{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg3.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg3.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{N}}={\mathbf{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t_{N}}={\mathbf{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>PRISM-Loop</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As we mentioned in Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Unconditional Text Generation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, the sentence diversity is crucial for unconditional generation, we observe that the vanilla PRISM inference from Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Employing PRISM at inference ‣ 3 PRISM ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> can degrade diversity.
we therefore employ PRISM-loop, analogous to ReMDM-loop <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, where we <em id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">extend</em> the standard generation process with a terminal refinement phase. After the initial generation of a sequence, an additional <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">looping</em> steps are performed. In each of these steps, a fixed-size subset of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> tokens is randomly selected from the full sequence, remasked, and subsequently unmasked to allow for iterative refinement.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg4" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 4</span> </span> PRISM inference with loop strategy</figcaption>
<div id="alg4.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg4.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Require:</span> Fine-tuned MDM with unmasking posterior model <math id="alg4.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, per-token quality head <math id="alg4.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;" mathcolor="#009F86">θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, sampling steps <math id="alg4.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, sequence length <math id="alg4.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, discretized time steps <math id="alg4.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{t_{\ell}\}_{\ell=0}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{t_{\ell}\}_{\ell=0}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, remasking token ratio <math id="alg4.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, loop steps <math id="alg4.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>,
number of remasking tokens at the loop stage <math id="alg4.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            Sample <math id="alg4.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg4.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg4.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> steps with PRISM with <math id="alg4.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg4.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg4.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> 

</div>
<div id="alg4.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              Uniformly sample size <math id="alg4.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> subset <math id="alg4.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}\subset\{0,\dots,L-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}\subset\{0,\dots,L-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg4.l5.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#009F86;">Remask</span> <math id="alg4.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{i}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{i}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="alg4.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg4.l6.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;">Unmask</span> <math id="alg4.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{i}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{i}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg4.l6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v^{i}\sim{\color[rgb]{0.2539,0.4102,0.8828}f_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\,|\,{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">i</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#4169E1">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" fence="false" mathcolor="#4169E1" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">𝐱</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4169E1;" mathcolor="#4169E1" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{i}\sim{\color[rgb]{0.2539,0.4102,0.8828}f_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\,|\,{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="alg4.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg4.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Experiment details and ablation studies</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides additional experimental details.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Omitted Results</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we present the comprehensive results on OpenWebText, on MAUVE score, Generative Perplexity (Gen PPL), and Entropy. The graph in Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.2 Unconditional Text Generation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is derived from Table <a href="#A4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ D.1 Omitted Results ‣ Appendix D Experiment details and ablation studies ‣ Fine-Tuning Masked Diffusion for ProvableSelf-Correction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, PRISM-loop for <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&gt;128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&gt;128</annotation></semantics></math> and PRISM for <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=128</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Evaluation result for PRISM-loop/PRISM/baselines. The best MAUVE scores are <span id="A4.T2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bolded</span>.</figcaption>
